":"2ce57447-5a19-451d-b6f4-3c0901d15d51","slug":"islandlk","factuality":"unknown"}},{"url":"https://www.us-inquirer.com/story/trump-announces-prisoner-swap-in-3-day-russia-ukraine-ceasefire/","articleId":null,"date":"2026-05-08T20:04:30.000Z","isOpinion":false,"sourceInfo":{"id":"bbe29ef5-975e-498e-910d-c18af0b8fea3","icon":"https://groundnews.b-cdn.net/assets/letterIcons/square/FFAB00/U.png","bias":"unknown","name":"us-inquirer.com","place":[{"id":"OklahomaCity,OklahomaCounty,OK,US","name":"Oklahoma City","type":"locality"},{"id":"OklahomaCounty,OK,US","name":"Oklahoma County","type":"administrative_area_level_2"},{"id":"OK,US","name":"Oklahoma","type":"administrative_area_level_1"},{"id":"US","name":"United States","type":"country"}],"interestId":"2b7978d1-9f3a-4187-9cdc-59c97fa730a0","slug":"us-inquirercom","factuality":"unknown"}},{"url":"https://www.wbap.com/2026/05/08/trump-says-russia-and-ukraine-have-agreed-to-his-request-for-a-3-day-ceasefire-and-a-prisoner-swap/","articleId":null,"date":"2026-05-09T04:53:27.000Z","isOpinion":false,"sourceInfo":{"id":"640590a4-3c21-4cfa-b9ac-68cd7644e746","icon":"https://groundnews.b-cdn.net/assets/letterIcons/square/00C853/W.png","bias":"right","name":"wbap.com","place":[],"interestId":"ddd1f66d-aba3-4896-a3eb-24fa60126fba","slug":"wbapcom","factuality":"mixed"}},{"url":"https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trump-announces-surprise-three-day-ceasefire-russia-ukraine-war","articleId":null,"date":"2026-05-08T18:23:00.000Z","isOpinion":false,"sourceInfo":{"id":"e4ef633a-0dd5-4a46-b709-0634df757650","icon":"https://groundnews.b-cdn.net/interests/560047740fe00d0c6d88ff0f55abb31926faf918.jpg","bias":"right","name":"Fox News","place":[{"id":"NewYork,NY,US","name":"New York","type":"locality"},{"id":"NY,US","name":"New York","type":"administrative_area_level_1"},{"id":"US","name":"United States","type":"country"}],"interestId":"ff76f69e-7b5d-42df-b9f4-ef26a9e5c9b0","slug":"fox-news_a44aba","factuality":"mixed"}},{"url":"https://www.breitbart.com/politics/2026/05/08/donald-trump-announces-3-day-ceasefire-prisoner-swap-russia-ukraine/","articleId":null,"date":"2026-05-08T21:12:55.000Z","isOpinion":false,"sourceInfo":{"id":"ac8e9e00-fb5a-4048-a431-14a09c72d397","icon":"https://groundnews.b-cdn.net/interests/9f29a3d3f02a0d13a629834288381c5c93fcb86f.jpg","bias":"right","name":"Breitbart","place":[{"id":"US","name":"United States","type":"country"}],"interestId":"2cbad193-1ff0-4a8d-9192-6ccdafa8284f","slug":"breitbart","factuality":"mixed"}}],"chatGptSummaries":{"right":"0. Russia and Ukraine agreed to a three-day ceasefire from May 9 to May 11, brokered by President Donald J. Trump, coinciding with Victory Day commemorations and including a complete suspension of hostilities on the battlefield.\n1. Both countries committed to exchanging 1,000 prisoners of war each as part of this agreement, marking a significant humanitarian exchange during the conflict.\n2. President Trump described the ceasefire as potentially the beginning of the end of the long and deadly war, following negotiations that involved direct talks with the leaders of both nations.\n3. The truce is monitored by international observers and represents the most significant pause in the fighting since the invasion began.","rightSummaryId":100136903,"analysis":"1. Left-leaning outlets frame the three-day ceasefire and 1,000-for-1,000 prisoner swap as a bilateral \"agree[ment]\" between Russia and Ukraine, using skeptical \"says\" to question Trump's mediation while tying it to Russia's Victory Day as potentially benefiting Putin.\n2. Right-leaning coverage counters with triumphant tones, hailing Trump's \"surprise\" \"Diplomatic Win\" and critiquing the \"Soviet\" parade, emphasizing his decisive role.\n3. Pivotal divides emerge over Trump's personal requests—de-emphasized left, spotlighted right—and past failed truces.\n4. Center-leaning reports neutrally \"announce\" and \"confirm\" without hype or doubt.\n5. All agree on dates, swap scale, and Zelenskyy/Ushakov validations, underscoring ideological rifts on Trump's diplomacy versus Russian motives.","analysisSummaryId":100136417,"left":"0. US President Donald Trump announced a three-day ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine from May 9 to May 11, coinciding with Russia's Victory Day celebrations, including a prisoner swap of 1,000 prisoners from each side.\n1. Trump stated that both Russian President Vladimir Putin and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky agreed to this ceasefire proposal, which includes a suspension of all kinetic activity.\n2. Despite the ceasefire announcement, hostilities continued with accusations of violations from both sides, including drone attacks and military responses.\n3. Peace talks remain deadlocked, but US-brokered negotiations continue, with efforts to revive discussions involving Ukrainian negotiators and US representatives.","leftSummaryId":100131632,"center":"$81","centerSummaryId":100130727},"relatedStoryIds":[]},"showOwnershipData":false,"children":"$L82"}]}]}],false,"$L83","$L84"]}]
